for S-Ventures plc as we establish ourselves as a focused investment company following the completion of the reverse takeover of our former operating subsidiaries into AIM-listed Tooru plc."]},{"type":"p","children":["We retain a significant shareholding in Tooru plc and are encouraged by the progress being made across its portfolio of consumer brands. During the period, we also made an investment in an innovative drone technology business, reflecting our intention to diversify our investment portfolio."]},{"type":"p","children":["Looking ahead, we intend to pursue further investment opportunities, particularly through convertible loan notes, which we believe can provide attractive potential returns alongside participation in the future growth of investee companies."]},{"type":"p","children":["Following the reverse takeover, our balance sheet reflects our transition from an operating group to an investment company. We are focused on maintaining a lean corporate structure and reducing overheads to ensure that resources are directed towards creating shareholder value."]},{"type":"p","children":["We have also been progressing a change of corporate adviser as we remain committed to our listing on the AQSE Growth Market. While the benefits of being publicly quoted have been limited in recent years, we believe that maintaining our listing, alongside a significantly reduced cost base, provides a platform for future growth."]},{"type":"p","children":["We recognise that conditions in the UK small-cap market have been challenging and that we have not been able to deliver the short-term returns our shareholders would have wished."]},{"type":"p","children":["Nevertheless, we believe that our existing investments, combined with a disciplined approach to new opportunities and cost management, provide a foundation for creating long-term shareholder value."]},{"type":"p","children":["I would like to thank our shareholders for their continued patience and support as we move into this next phase of the Company's development\"."]},{"type":"p","children":["This announcement contains inside information as stipulated under the UK version of the Market Abuse Regulation No 596/2014 which is part of English Law by virtue of the European (Withdrawal) Act 2018, as amended. On publication of this announcement via a Regulatory Information Service, this information is considered to be in the public domain."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Enquiries"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["S-Ventures PLC"]},{"type":"p","children":["Scott Livingston, Chief Executive Officer"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+44 (0)20 3475 0230"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Oberon Investments (Broker)"]},{"type":"p","children":["Nick Lovering"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["+44 (0) 20 3179 5300"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Interim management report"]},{"type":"p","children":["For this period the Company has acted as a cash shell which, under Aquis Rules, means it is an enterprise company. The principal assets of the Company are comprised of a 24.04% holding of ordinary shares in Tooru plc and a minority shareholding in Hybrid Drones Limited."]},{"type":"p","children":["By order of the Board"]},{"type":"p","children":["Scott Livingston"]},{"type":"p","children":["Chief Executive Officer"]},{"type":"p","children":["30 September 2026"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Cautionary statement"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["This report contains forward-looking statements. These have been made by the directors in good faith based on the information available to them up to the time of their approval of this report. The directors can give no assurance that these expectations will prove to